 "description": "T-5483: what a custom Product subtotal shows where its line meets the grand-total column. gen-pivot ec473260bb2065b3 P05 shows 0 there on all 63 lines, each with one of three item columns filled, where the item column shows the product; a custom Min shows the minimum in both (pivots.md \"What the gen-pivot batch found\"). Each sheet is one builder-v2 pivot at A3 over Data!A1:E11 (Region, Product, Size, Val, Kind; ten records), rows Region then Product, columns Size, Sum of Val unless said. East and West have records in both sizes and North in S only, so a rule that reads an empty item column as 0 gives 0 for North alone, and a rule that is 0 at every grand-total column gives 0 for all three. P1: the one function Product on Region, on the item's own line (compact). P2: Product and Min, whose lines follow the children. P3: Product in tabular form. P4: columns Size then Kind, for Size's default subtotal columns. P5: the function on a column field (rows Size, columns Region, Product), for the row grand total. P6: Product as the data field's own function, no custom subtotal. P7: the custom Product over an Average data field. PV: the shape of the evidence sheet, as a control: the Values field outermost on rows (rows Values, Region, Product) over StdDevp, Min and Sum of Val, the one function Product on Region. FSum: the one function sum. FCouA: the one function countA. FAvg: the one function avg. FMax: the one function max. FStd: the one function stdDev. FVar: the one function var.",
